<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 23.06 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 23.06 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bewllether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 23 basis points to 23.06 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of 10 Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     23.28	    23.06		   - 22 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     26.75	    26.20		   - 55 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    28.16	    27.33		   - 83 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     28.03	    27.37		   - 66 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 local time/1930 EDT).</p>
<p>-- Patricia Lezama, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289554</p>
</text>
